### What is the Longest Palindromic Subsequence?

A palindromic subsequence is a sequence of characters from the string that reads the same forwards and backwards, but the characters need not be contiguous. The longest palindromic subsequence (LPS) is the one with the maximum length.

For example, in the string "ABRACADABRA", one palindromic subsequence is "ABAABA" (length 6). Characters are picked from various positions but maintain their relative order.

In banking, the National Bank of India uses reference codes on transactions, and a compliance system flags codes with long palindromic patterns as potential markers for suspicious activity.

### How does the interval DP work?

Define `dp[i][j]` as the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the substring from index i to index j inclusive. Fill the table by increasing interval length so that smaller intervals are always ready before larger ones.

- Base case: `dp[i][i] = 1` because a single character is a palindrome of length 1.
- If `s.charAt(i) == s.charAt(j)`, the two ends match and wrap the inner palindrome: `dp[i][j] = dp[i+1][j-1] + 2`.
- If `s.charAt(i) != s.charAt(j)`, drop one end: `dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])`.

The answer is `dp[0][n-1]`, covering the entire string.

```java
package com.bank.service;

public class PalindromePatternDetector {

    public static int longestPalindromicSubsequence(String code) {
        int n = code.length();
        int[][] dp = new int[n][n];

        // Base case: single characters
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            dp[i][i] = 1;
        }

        // Fill by increasing interval length
        for (int len = 2; len <= n; len++) {
            for (int i = 0; i <= n - len; i++) {
                int j = i + len - 1;
                if (code.charAt(i) == code.charAt(j)) {
                    dp[i][j] = dp[i + 1][j - 1] + 2;
                } else {
                    dp[i][j] = Math.max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1]);
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[0][n - 1];
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String refCode = "NBIABCBA";
        System.out.println("LPS length: " + longestPalindromicSubsequence(refCode));
    }
}
```

